Expected elements: present

No MUST-SHOW item absent, no MUST-NOT item present. A dense, optically well-centred tool surface whose widest column is its emptiest.

Pane fade (a): it works; do not lengthen it. The ramp is a fixed 24px anchored to the pane bottom (black leaves at y=1051, border 1075) — one 23px line. In Code, 16 of those px land on glyph rows, so line 61 is half-dissolved and reads as continuation, not a cut. The 2.19:1 figure is that line's y=1066 tail; the same line is 9.2:1 at cap height — the affordance working, not a legibility failure. A longer ramp dims a second line in a register where density is the virtue. The third lens is right only about surfaces: the mask washes the RAW (CHAIN-NATIVE) block's #000 to #1a1a1a against a #1b1b1b pane, so its edges (x=1543/1905) vanish 10px early. Overlay each scroller in its own colour instead.

Re-measurement holds. Columns 913/608/383. Tabbed region interior 605px, last content y=322 → 346px empty (57.2%); Values 405px, 122px empty (30.1%). Column content totals 542px of 1010, so no row re-split recovers any of the 468px void — the row split is provably not the lever. Call Trace's widest row wastes 152px horizontally (path ends 1353, opcodes start 1505); Values wastes 158px. Code meanwhile hard-clips line 40 mid-identifier at x=916 with no fade; Transaction wraps 42-char hashes.

Top fixes: move ~150px of middle-column width to Code and Transaction; give Code a right-edge overflow signal.

Rating: 6/10

